.TH "BROWSE" "1" "" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
browse - A multi-file pager with recursive navigation.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
browse [-fFinv] [-p pattern] [-t title] [filename\&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Browse and search text files, follow changes.
.PP
In contrast to conventional pagers, \f[B]browse\f[R] allows the current
file set to be suspended temporarily while a different set of files is
examined, and then restored at the prior location.
This recursive model supports investigation of logs, search results,
source trees, and related materials without discarding context.
.PP
Conceptually, the program may be understood as combining the behavior of
\f[V]less\f[R] with a stack-based file navigation model similar to
\f[V]pushd\f[R]/\f[V]popd\f[R].
.SS Overview
.IP \[bu] 2
Supports examination of multiple files within a single workflow.
.IP \[bu] 2
Allows temporary transition to a new file set and later return to the
prior position.
.IP \[bu] 2
Accepts command output from pipelines as browsable input.
.IP \[bu] 2
Provides keyboard-driven navigation, search, shell access, and history.
.IP \[bu] 2
Preserves context during analysis of logs, source code, and generated
output.
.SS Features
.SS Navigation
.IP \[bu] 2
Forward and reverse paging.
.IP \[bu] 2
Continuous scrolling in both directions.
.IP \[bu] 2
Horizontal scrolling for wide lines.
.IP \[bu] 2
Jump to line numbers.
.IP \[bu] 2
Mark pages and return to them.
.IP \[bu] 2
Follow and tail modes for changing files.
.SS Search and Exploration
.IP \[bu] 2
Forward and reverse regex and fixed-string search.
.IP \[bu] 2
Case-sensitive and case-insensitive search.
.IP \[bu] 2
Pattern highlighting.
.IP \[bu] 2
Search pattern history.
.IP \[bu] 2
Run \f[V]grep\f[R] on the current file in a nested browse session.
.SS Multi-File Operation
.IP \[bu] 2
Browse multiple files from the command line.
.IP \[bu] 2
Browse standard input as a temporary file.
.IP \[bu] 2
Open nested file sets with \f[V]B\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
Return from nested file sets with \f[V]x\f[R] or \f[V]X\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
Rewind the active file list with \f[V]Ctrl+R\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
Show the current remaining file list with \f[V]a\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
Show the suspended browse stack with \f[V]A\f[R].
.SS Additional Facilities
.IP \[bu] 2
File and directory completion.
.IP \[bu] 2
Shell escape with command completion.
.IP \[bu] 2
Persistent file, directory, search, and shell histories.
.IP \[bu] 2
Session saving and restoration.
.IP \[bu] 2
Transparent browsing of compressed files.
.IP \[bu] 2
Run \f[V]fmt -s\f[R] on the current file in a nested browse session.
.IP \[bu] 2
Built-in help screen.
.SS Continuous Scrolling and Following
.PP
\f[B]browse\f[R] supports continuous scrolling and file following:
.IP \[bu] 2
Continuous scrolling moves upward or downward until interrupted.
Use \f[V]d\f[R] to scroll toward EOF and \f[V]u\f[R] to scroll toward
SOF.
.IP \[bu] 2
When continuous scrolling reaches EOF, \f[B]browse\f[R] enters follow
mode and displays lines appended to the file.
.IP \[bu] 2
The tail command jumps to EOF and follows subsequent output from that
point.
.IP \[bu] 2
The cursor indicates whether follow mode is active.
In follow mode, the cursor is in the lower-left corner; otherwise, it is
in the upper-left corner.
.SS Usage
.PP
Browse one or more files:
.nf

browse file1.log file2.log file3.log
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Browse shell-expanded globs:
.nf

browse *.go
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Browse results from a pipeline:
.nf

grep -rl timeout /var/log | browse
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Start with an initial search pattern:
.nf

browse -p ERROR app.log
\f[R]
.fi
.SS Command Line Options
.nf

browse [OPTIONS] [FILE] [FILE...]
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
.ne 12v
