.PP
If the required decompressor is not installed, \f[B]browse\f[R] displays
an error and skips the file rather than attempting to render raw binary
data.
.PP
The original compressed filename is recorded in the file history and
session file, so it can be reopened later from the \f[V]B\f[R] prompt or
during a subsequent launch.
.PP
\f[B]Limitation:\f[R] \f[V]Ctrl+R\f[R] (rewind list) does not work while
browsing a compressed file.
The content is decompressed once into a temporary stream; rewinding is
not supported in that session.
.SS Changing Directory
.PP
Press \f[V]C\f[R] to change the current working directory.
The prompt accepts \f[V]\[ti]\f[R], \f[V]-\f[R], and \f[V]\[ti]-\f[R],
quoted directory names, and \f[V]%\f[R] for the parent directory of the
current file.
Directory completion includes entries from \f[V]CDPATH\f[R].
.SS Symbol Expansions
.PP
