.TE
.SS Configuration and History
.PP
\f[B]browse\f[R] stores configuration and history in:
.nf

\[ti]/.browse/
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
The session file is:
.nf

\[ti]/.browse/browserc
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Stored session data includes:
.IP \[bu] 2
Current file name.
.IP \[bu] 2
First line on the page.
.IP \[bu] 2
Search pattern.
.IP \[bu] 2
Marks.
.IP \[bu] 2
Page title.
.IP \[bu] 2
Search case-sensitivity mode.
.IP \[bu] 2
Fixed-string search mode.
.PP
History files are maintained for common workflows, with behavior similar
to Bash history:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Shell commands\f[R] (\f[V]!\f[R] key): Every shell command is
recorded and can be recalled, edited, and rerun.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Directory history\f[R] (\f[V]C\f[R] key): Recently visited
directories are recorded for efficient navigation across large projects.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]File history\f[R] (\f[V]B\f[R] prompt): Browsed files are saved as
full pathnames and remain available in current and future sessions.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Search patterns\f[R] (\f[V]/\f[R] and \f[V]?\f[R] prompts): Regex
and text search patterns are saved so they can be repeated or revisited
without retyping them.
.PP
History files:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]\[ti]/.browse/browse_dirs\f[R] - directory history.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]\[ti]/.browse/browse_files\f[R] - file browsing history.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]\[ti]/.browse/browse_search\f[R] - search pattern history.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]\[ti]/.browse/browse_shell\f[R] - shell command history.
.SS Limitations
.IP \[bu] 2
Xterm-specific behavior.
.IP \[bu] 2
Displayed lines are clipped to screen width, with horizontal scrolling
available for wider lines.
.IP \[bu] 2
Long lines are internally capped at about 4K.
.IP \[bu] 2
Tabs are converted to spaces.
.IP \[bu] 2
Non-printable characters may display poorly.
.IP \[bu] 2
Terminal title handling may vary by environment.
